<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<section xml:id="dimensions-overview" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>The Six Dimensions of Culturally Responsive Teaching</title>

  <introduction>
    <figure xml:id="Diagram-Six-DimensionsCRT">
      <caption>The six dimensions of culturally responsive teaching</caption>
      <image source="Diagram-Six-DimensionsCRT.png">
        <shortdescription>Six numbered hexagons ringing a center labeled Youth empowerment, each pointing inward.</shortdescription>
        <description>
          <p>
            Six colored hexagons are arranged in a ring, numbered 1 through 6: Students at the
            Center, Relationships and caring, Deep thinking, Access and relevance, Social justice
            reflection, and Inclusion through cultural diversity. An arrow points inward from each
            hexagon to a green splash at the center labeled <q>Youth empowerment</q>, which is
            encircled by a band labeled <q>Curriculum</q>.
          </p>
        </description>
      </image>
    </figure>
    <p>
      These six dimensions aim to capture the essence of Culturally Responsive Teaching in our
      informal math enrichment program (and we believe that can be helpful for other programs).
      Each dimension corresponds to a hexagon in the diagram. We also describe the
      <q>fundamental goal</q> of our program (in the center of the diagram), as well as the three
      general contexts in which the six dimensions materialize (the concentric circles).
    </p>

    <p>
      <dl>
        <li><title>The main goal</title>
          <p>Personal Development &amp; Growth</p>
        </li>
        <li><title>The three contexts</title>
          <p>Program structure, Pedagogical practices, Curriculum</p>
        </li>
        <li><title>The six dimensions</title>
          <p>
            <ol>
              <li>Students at the center</li>
              <li>Relationships and caring</li>
              <li>Deep thinking</li>
              <li>Access and relevance</li>
              <li>Inclusion through cultural diversity</li>
              <li>Social justice reflection</li>
            </ol>
          </p>
        </li>
      </dl>
    </p>

  </introduction>

